{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgxk6n4MoeFKNVBx7VXrC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The IV estimate is about **8.53%** more wage per additional year of schooling.\n\nI used two-stage least squares with the Q4 birth indicator as the instrument for `years_of_schooling`. I treated `year_of_birth` and `state_of_birth` as categorical controls (one dummy per year and per state, 51 states), since they are codes rather than quantities. The coefficient on schooling is 0.0853 on log wage, so it reads as 8.53% per year. The standard error is 0.0255, which is about 2.55 percentage points.\n\nIf you treat year and state as continuous, the estimate falls to about 7.52%. I went with the categorical version because it is the usual specification for this data (Angrist and Krueger, 1991).\n\nANSWER: 8.53"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1083,"cache_read_input_tokens":32391,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1083},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db0ef042-c854-4959-8143-34b6629747de","uuid":"717d93d7-7ba9-4b30-a73d-2972a55ef65b","timestamp":"2026-11-12T08:47:48.148Z","request_id":"req_011Cgxk6mpDhqpotUXHYonuK"}
